---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import brokerOverview from "../assets/hmi-overview.webp";
import mqttUsers from "../assets/hmi-users.webp";
import deployPanel from "../assets/hmi-deploy.webp";

const repoURL = "https://github.com/fgjcarlos/mcm";

const quickStart = [
  { label: "Clone and build", code: "git clone https://github.com/fgjcarlos/mcm.git && cd mcm && task build" },
  { label: "Start the development stack", code: "task up" },
  { label: "Find the initial administrator sign-in", code: "task logs    # first-boot credentials are printed here when generated" },
];

const stack = ["Go 1.25", "SQLite", "Mosquitto", "React 19 + Vite 8", "REST + WebSocket API"];
---

<Layout
  title="MCM — Mosquitto Control Manager"
  description="MCM is a self-hosted administration interface for an existing Mosquitto broker. See what is available in the alpha and try it locally."
>
  <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <header class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <span class="rounded-full border border-signal-bright/30 bg-signal/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-signal-pale">Alpha</span>
        <span class="rounded-full border border-hairline bg-surface px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-ink-soft">Apache 2.0</span>
        <a class="text-xs font-medium text-ink-soft underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-ink-bright hover:underline" href={`${repoURL}/actions/workflows/ci.yml`} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Image CI workflow</a>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-5">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-signal-bright">Mosquitto Control Manager</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-bright sm:text-6xl">Manage a Mosquitto broker from the web.</h1>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft sm:text-xl">
          Mosquitto is the server that routes MQTT messages between devices. MCM adds a browser interface and API to manage one Mosquitto broker; Mosquitto continues to handle the messages.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-signal-pale/90">Alpha: useful configuration controls are available today, while the graphical configuration interface is still incomplete.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-signal px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-floor transition hover:bg-signal-bright focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-signal-outline" href="#quick-start">
          Try locally <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
        </a>
        <a class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center rounded-full border border-hairline-strong bg-surface px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink transition hover:border-hairline-bright hover:text-ink-bright focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-signal-outline" href={repoURL} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="mt-20 space-y-8" aria-labelledby="availability-title">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-signal-bright">Availability</p>
        <h2 id="availability-title" class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-bright">What you can change today—and what remains.</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">The current alpha manages one Mosquitto broker. The available controls are real; coverage and production readiness are not complete.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="rounded-3xl border border-hairline bg-surface p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink-bright">Available controls</h3>
          <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            <li>MQTT users and basic access control lists (ACLs): rules for which message topics each user can access.</li>
            <li>Listeners: network ports where the broker accepts device connections; broker TLS certificates and keys to secure those connections.</li>
            <li>General broker settings and bridges: connections that pass messages between brokers.</li>
            <li>Plugins, including Dynamic Security: Mosquitto's plugin for managing users and access rules.</li>
            <li>Advanced editing of the main <code class="font-mono text-signal-pale">mosquitto.conf</code> configuration file.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Applying changes requires a fresh multi-factor authentication (MFA) check: enter a new code from your authenticator app.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-3xl border border-hairline bg-surface p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink-bright">Remaining work</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Broader native ACL coverage, complete backup and restore (<a class="underline decoration-hairline-soft underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink-bright" href={`${repoURL}/issues/295`}>#295</a>), and an explicit Mosquitto version support matrix remain unfinished. Some configuration directives and included files are not editable through guided controls.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-3xl border border-hairline bg-surface p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink-bright">Known limitations</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">SQLite is the only implemented management database. Observed traffic is not a full client inventory. Sparkplug B and JSON Schema diagnostics inspect messages for issues but never block or reject them. Fleets, multi-broker management, single sign-on (SSO), high availability, and PostgreSQL are deferred. The dashboard's Broker diagnostics workspace reports the broker's own view of connections, logs and metrics.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20 space-y-8" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-signal-bright">Product evidence</p>
        <h2 id="evidence-title" class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-bright">Review, apply, verify.</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Real captures from a running MCM local stack. Select any image to inspect its full-size file.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-hairline bg-surface-panel">
        <a class="block focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-signal-outline" href={deployPanel.src} aria-label="Open full-size MCM deploy panel capture">
          <img class="block h-auto w-full" src={deployPanel.src} width={deployPanel.width} height={deployPanel.height} alt="MCM deploy panel showing configuration preview controls and deployment history with a verified activation entry." loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <figcaption class="border-t border-hairline px-5 py-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          <p>Deploy panel: preview configuration changes before applying them. Sensitive changes require a fresh authenticator code. The history verifies activation when a probe succeeds; here, entry 3 was verified by a user-grant probe.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">Entry 2 rolled back because no activation probe was available: the configured managed service account lacked a user read/write grant. Entry 1 failed during apply and restored the saved snapshot. These records show both recovery paths, not only successful deployment. <a class="underline decoration-hairline-soft underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink-bright" href={deployPanel.src}>Open full-size capture</a>.</p>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <figure class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-hairline bg-surface-panel">
          <a class="block focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-signal-outline" href={brokerOverview.src} aria-label="Open full-size broker overview capture">
            <img class="block h-auto w-full" src={brokerOverview.src} width={brokerOverview.width} height={brokerOverview.height} alt="MCM broker overview showing connection status, observed message rate and top topics." loading="lazy" />
          </a>
          <figcaption class="border-t border-hairline px-5 py-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Broker overview: check the broker connection status, observed message rate, and top topics. Observed messages are not a complete client inventory. <a class="underline decoration-hairline-soft underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink-bright" href={brokerOverview.src}>Full-size</a>.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-hairline bg-surface-panel">
          <a class="block focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-signal-outline" href={mqttUsers.src} aria-label="Open full-size MQTT user directory capture">
            <img class="block h-auto w-full" src={mqttUsers.src} width={mqttUsers.width} height={mqttUsers.height} alt="MCM MQTT user directory showing user status and controls to disable an account or reset its password." loading="lazy" />
          </a>
          <figcaption class="border-t border-hairline px-5 py-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">MQTT user directory: check account status and available controls to disable a user or reset their password. <a class="underline decoration-hairline-soft underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink-bright" href={mqttUsers.src}>Full-size</a>.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20 rounded-3xl border border-caution/25 bg-caution-panel/10 p-6 sm:p-8" aria-labelledby="production-title">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-caution-soft">Caution</p>
      <h2 id="production-title" class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-caution-bright">Alpha software; review production limits before applying changes.</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Activation verification and recovery have known gaps, and backup/restore is incomplete. Review deployment requirements before enabling writes on an existing broker.</p>
      <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3 text-sm font-semibold text-signal-pale">
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href={`${repoURL}/issues/308`}>Configuration tracker</a>
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href={`${repoURL}/blob/main/docs/product-scope.md`}>Scope and acceptance criteria</a>
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href={`${repoURL}/blob/main/docs/production.md#current-limitations`}>Production limitations</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <details class="mt-12 rounded-3xl border border-hairline bg-surface-faint p-6">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-ink-strong">Technical stack</summary>
      <ul class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        {stack.map((item) => <li class="rounded-full border border-hairline bg-surface-chip px-3 py-1 font-mono text-xs text-signal-pale">{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">MCM's application includes the dashboard and management API; Mosquitto runs separately. SQLite is the only implemented management database.</p>
    </details>

    <section id="quick-start" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-8 rounded-3xl border border-hairline bg-surface-panel p-8 backdrop-blur" aria-labelledby="quick-start-title">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-signal-bright">Quick start</p>
      <h2 id="quick-start-title" class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-bright">Run the alpha locally.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">For this local development setup, install <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="https://git-scm.com/downloads">Git</a> to clone the source, <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="https://docs.docker.com/compose/install/">Docker Compose</a> to run the containers, and <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="https://taskfile.dev/installation/">Task</a> to run the project commands. These steps start a development stack, not a production deployment.</p>
      <ol class="mt-8 space-y-4">
        {quickStart.map((step, idx) => (
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-2 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:gap-6">
            <span class="inline-flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-signal-bright/40 bg-signal/10 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-signal-pale">{String(idx + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
            <div class="flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
              <span class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-ink-muted">{step.label}</span>
              <code class="block w-full overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-surface-code px-4 py-3 font-mono text-sm text-signal-pale">{step.code}</code>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-signal-bright/20 bg-signal/5 p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink-bright">Success checkpoint</h3>
        <ol class="mt-3 list-inside list-decimal space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          <li>Open <a class="font-mono text-signal-pale underline underline-offset-4" href="http://localhost:8080">http://localhost:8080</a>.</li>
          <li>Sign in with the initial administrator credentials printed in the first-start logs. The username is <code class="font-mono text-signal-pale">admin</code> unless <code class="font-mono text-signal-pale">MCM_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_USERNAME</code> was set; use the generated bootstrap password.</li>
          <li>Confirm the dashboard shows the broker as connected.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink-bright">No bootstrap credentials in the logs?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">There is no default password. If no generated credentials appear, check whether <code class="font-mono text-signal-pale">MCM_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_USERNAME</code> and <code class="font-mono text-signal-pale">MCM_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD</code> were set before first start, then use those values. Do not guess or reuse a broker password.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink-bright">Signed in, but the broker shows disconnected?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">In the dashboard you just opened, go to Diagnostics → Broker diagnostics to inspect connection status, broker logs, and diagnostic observations.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink-bright">Dashboard unreachable?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Run <code class="font-mono text-signal-pale">task ps</code> to check the services, then <code class="font-mono text-signal-pale">task logs</code> for startup errors. Confirm port 8080 is available and run <code class="font-mono text-signal-pale">task ready</code> to check readiness.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">Stop the stack with <code class="font-mono text-signal-pale">task down</code>. Read the <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href={`${repoURL}/blob/main/docs/production.md`}>Production deployment guide</a> for deployment requirements, broker TLS, and recovery limits.</p>
    </section>

    <footer class="mt-20 flex flex-col items-start justify-between gap-4 border-t border-hairline pt-8 text-sm text-ink-muted sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
      <p>© {new Date().getFullYear()} MCM contributors · Apache 2.0</p>
      <nav aria-label="Project resources" class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-3">
        <a class="hover:text-ink-bright" href={repoURL} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        <a class="hover:text-ink-bright" href={`${repoURL}/issues`} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Issues</a>
        <a class="hover:text-ink-bright" href={`${repoURL}/blob/main/docs/openapi.yaml`} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">OpenAPI spec</a>
        <a class="hover:text-ink-bright" href={`${repoURL}/blob/main/SECURITY.md`} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Security</a>
      </nav>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>
